From c0778bbbc65d1bb5f34fd92d432fab435cd816e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ecogamezz <33791269+ecogamezz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:34:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] WowCraft: the terrain cut, our Minecraft body and face,
 trader labels, partners and shadows

- The terrain cut: REN_CUT (cells full blocks fill) and REN_DUG (cells dug out of WoW's
  ground, per world) go into benilla_world::terrain_cut, a 128 x 64 x 128 bit volume round us
  in one storage buffer every terrain material binds (binding 91); terrain.wgsl drops its
  ground in a set cell. Empty and off without WowCraft. REN_SOLIDS is kept for what Minecraft's
  shadows fall on.
- mc_body: our Minecraft skin (WOWCRAFT_SKIN_FILE, or the texture Minecraft sends as ours) is
  our body on the character select and create stages, in place of the WoW model; Minecraft's
  skin processing (legacy widening, opaque base layer, slim arms) and its player model.
- head_portrait: the skin's face, with its hat layer, is the player portrait.
- labels: a green "Block trader (right-click)" under innkeepers and general goods vendors, and
  co-op partners' names over them, as camera-facing glyph meshes like the overhead names.
- WE_PLAYER: co-op partners near us; their WoW characters are hidden behind their Minecraft
  bodies. WE_SHADOW: Minecraft's soft entity shadows on blocks and WoW's ground.
- Hooks: the portrait sync set and the glue stage resource, the overhead names' mesh builder.

Verified: cargo test --release -p benilla-app --no-default-features --lib wowcraft (37),
-p wowcraft-link (8), -p benilla-world --lib terrain_cut (2); cargo build --release -p benilla
--no-default-features; a live run against the local vmangos (character select dump with the
body, and in the world with mod/test/CutMinecraft: 19 cells cut, no shader errors). Built on
macOS (Intel) only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
